    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Solve $\\cot x=\\sin 2x$ for $0^\\circ\\le x\\le360^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=45^\\circ,90^\\circ,135^\\circ,225^\\circ,270^\\circ,315^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "Since $\\cot x$ is defined only when $\\sin x\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}&=2\\sin x\\cos x\\\\\\cos x&=2\\sin^2x\\cos x\\\\\\cos x(1-2\\sin^2x)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence $\\cos x=0$ or $\\sin^2x=\\frac12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos x&=0,&x&=90^\\circ,270^\\circ\\\\\\sin x&=\\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2},&x&=45^\\circ,135^\\circ,225^\\circ,315^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nAll satisfy the original equation. Therefore $x=45^\\circ,90^\\circ,135^\\circ,225^\\circ,270^\\circ,315^\\circ$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
  },
